{"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep each record in a table of the app’s own GRDB database until it is delivered."}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"GRDBPersistence"}],"symbolKind":"module","title":"GRDBPersistence","roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","externalID":"GRDBPersistence"},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DatabaseStore"},{"type":"text","text":" is a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RecordStore"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") for apps on Apple platforms that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"already keep a GRDB database. It takes the app’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DatabaseQueue"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DatabasePool"},{"type":"text","text":" and a table"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"name, creates the table with a migration of its own, and opens no second SQLite database. It is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"product of its own, which "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves out."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It makes the same promises as ","type":"text"},{"code":"SegmentStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The tracker’s worker commits each record, in a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"transaction of its own, before publishing it. A batch’s rows are marked before any destination","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"receives it and deleted once every destination has. The table holds at most ","type":"text"},{"code":"byteBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" bytes of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"encoded records, 5 MiB by default, with the oldest rows deleted to make room, and each drop is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reported on ","type":"text"},{"code":"DatabaseStore.dropReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Records are encoded as ","type":"text"},{"code":"SegmentStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" encodes them, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only events of the types in ","type":"text"},{"code":"events","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which conform to ","type":"text"},{"code":"BinaryCodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", are kept.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"How durable a commit is against power loss is the database’s choice, through its journal mode and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"synchronous"},{"type":"text","text":" setting. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DatabaseStore.synchronize()"},{"type":"text","text":" checkpoints a database in WAL mode; call it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as the app moves to the background. Open one store per table at a time, and don’t open one from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inside an access to the same database."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An app with no database of its own uses "},{"code":"SegmentStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which needs no GRDB."}]},{"code":["import GRDB","import GRDBPersistence","","let database = try DatabaseQueue(path: databasePath)","let store = try DatabaseStore(events: [SignedUp.self], database: database, table: \"analyticsRecord\")","let tracker = Tracker(store: store)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: vendor)","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers what a store keeps, its bounds and recovery."}]},{"anchor":"API","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"API"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The documentation site is built on Linux, where this module’s API isn’t there, so its symbols","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"have no pages of their own here. Their doc comments are in the sources, and Xcode shows them","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for an Apple target.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Keeping-records-in-a-database","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Keeping records in a database"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DatabaseStore"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/grdbpersistence"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://GRDBPersistence/documentation/GRDBPersistence":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep each record in a table of the app’s own GRDB database until it is delivered."}],"role":"collection","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/grdbpersistence","title":"GRDBPersistence","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence":{"url":"\/documentation\/persistence","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so the records a tracker tracked survive the app ending.","type":"text"}],"title":"Persistence","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/persistingrecords":{"type":"link","title":"Persisting Records","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Persisting Records","type":"text"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords"}}}